invariant: INV-16
file: ct.h
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: ct.h gives every file of a WIDEMUL=runtime object the native multiply,
  so the files under their own names, which the answer
  CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED and every refused byte run, are the native copies
  again under other names. Every test that checks bytes passes, and the
  dispatch counts still split by name. test/widemul-builds.sh requires
  each file under its own names to compile to the same assembly with the
  runtime define as without it.

--- old
#if (defined(CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL) || defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE_COPY)) && !defined(CH_CT_WIDEMUL)
--- new
#if (defined(CH_NATIVE_WIDEMUL) || defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE_COPY) || defined(CH_WIDEMUL_RUNTIME)) && !defined(CH_CT_WIDEMUL)
